KIND=build_fail
ERR=logs.Size undefined
NOTE=.Size() needs a receiver type the transpiler can resolve from the .gala file's own text. A receiver whose type is written out resolves even when the type is declared in another package as a GALA struct; a receiver whose type is inferred from a call does not, even when that call returns a GALA-declared type in the same package. A multi-value binding cannot be annotated to pin the type, so `var logs []Log, err = listLogs()` is a parse error and no spelling recovers it. That is what makes this a boundary gap and not the receiver-resolution defect filed separately: there is a way to name the type in principle and no way to name it here. Blocks any file counting the elements of a slice returned by a Go function. Pinned to the GALA release by construction; re-baseline with the procedure in docs/gala-translation.md under "When to revisit"
